FG-021: lo_setDocumentPassword refuses a URL with no pending load instead of dereferencing end().

lo_setDocumentPassword looks the URL up in mInteractionMap and only assert()s that it
is there. assert() is compiled out of release builds (NDEBUG), so a URL that no load is
waiting on dereferences end(): undefined behaviour, in practice memory corruption, not
an error. The bridge answers LOK_CALLBACK_DOCUMENT_PASSWORD with the key it computes for
its own load (getAbsoluteURL), so this should never happen; this makes a mismatch fail
safely if it ever does. The load then aborts through the interaction handler as usual.

Not EMSCRIPTEN-guarded: it is a plain upstream bug, written up for upstream in
upstream-issues/ (agents never post; the owner submits).

--- a/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
@@ -7863,7 +7863,13 @@
     assert(pURL);
     LibLibreOffice_Impl *const pLib = static_cast<LibLibreOffice_Impl*>(pThis);
     auto it = pLib->mInteractionMap.find(OString(pURL));
-    assert(it != pLib->mInteractionMap.end());
+    // assert() is compiled out of release builds, where a URL with no pending
+    // interaction would dereference end(). Refuse it instead.
+    if (it == pLib->mInteractionMap.end())
+    {
+        SAL_WARN("lok", "setDocumentPassword: no document load is waiting for a password at this URL");
+        return;
+    }
     it->second->SetPassword(pPassword);
 }
 
